Ported code
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

CHIRP (https://github.com/kk7ds/chirp)
  Copyright 2012 Dan Smith and CHIRP contributors. GPL-2.0-or-later.
  The UV-5R clone protocol (identification magics, block read and write, firmware probe,
  dropped byte workaround), the memory map, the 16 byte channel and name record layout, the
  tone and DCS encoding, the model identification tables (chirp/drivers/uv5r.py), the CTCSS and
  DCS code tables (chirp/chirp_common.py), the .img metadata trailer (chirp_common.py
  CloneModeRadio) and the CSV column semantics (chirp/drivers/generic_csv.py) are ported to
  Kotlin in the protocol module. Reference revision: d3bed431003087948b17bf15d09c53ad7dbbeec5.

CHIRP Baofeng DM-32UV driver (chirp/drivers/baofeng_dm32uv.py)
  Copyright 2026 chaffed. GPL-3.0-or-later.
  The DM-32UV image layout, channel record, Kenwood tone encoding, zone, scan list and TX contact
  editing, and clone protocol are ported to Kotlin in the protocol module (Dm32uv*.kt). The test
  image protocol/src/test/resources/fixtures/chirp-dm32uv.img is CHIRP's
  tests/images/Baofeng_DM-32UV.img. Reference revision: d99bb227093a0191a973ab9aa17276a0bee7b00a.

Radtel-RT950-Pro-Firmware (https://github.com/Hertzz58/Radtel-RT950-Pro-Firmware)
  GPL-3.0. The RT-950 Pro clone protocol (handshake, key table, key frame, XOR rules, read and
  write commands) is ported from tools/cps_flash.py (Rt950Pro*.kt). Reference revision:
  b49804bafcf86271fdb8b20f9a32b7d30d5ea1be.

Chirp_Radtel-RT-950-Pro (https://github.com/NathanBarguss/Chirp_Radtel-RT-950-Pro)
  The RT-950 Pro segment list and order, the 32 byte channel record, the DCS table, bands and
  power levels come from rt950pro/transport.py, channel.py, image.py, chirp_driver.py and
  DESIGN.md (Rt950Pro*.kt). Test expected values were computed with this code. Reference
  revision: 254d2cd52e152a83cdc2f008e26afd7ed03b2798. License:

