Data sources
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Hearham (https://hearham.com): repeater data from Hearham.com. A snapshot of the public API
  response, trimmed to the records and fields Offset uses, ships in the app
  (app/src/main/assets/repeaters/hearham.json.gz, date in hearham.meta.json), and a small extract
  is a unit test fixture (app/src/test/resources/hearham-fixture.json).
IRLP (https://status.irlp.net): "Node data from the IRLP status page". Node callsign, frequency,
  offset, access tone, location and last report time for nodes that reported within 30 days, from
  the public node status list, ship in app/src/main/assets/repeaters/listings.json.gz (date in
  listings.meta.json).
OpenStreetMap (https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright): repeater listings © OpenStreetMap
  contributors. The extract in app/src/main/assets/repeaters/listings.json.gz (records with
  "src":"OSM") is a derived database of OpenStreetMap data and is made available under the Open
  Database License 1.0 (https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/). Anyone may use, copy and
  redistribute that extract under the ODbL; it is produced by scripts/update_listings_bundle.py.
US Census Bureau Gazetteer, 2025 (https://www.census.gov/geographies/reference-files/time-series/geo/gazetteer-files.html):
  county names and internal points, public domain (US government work). File:
  app/src/main/assets/places/counties.tsv.
RepeaterBook (https://www.repeaterbook.com): "Data courtesy of RepeaterBook.com". No
  RepeaterBook data is stored in this repository; the RepeaterBook test fixture is synthetic.
